<!-- =============================== GLOSSARY =============================== -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2 id="t-the-words">The Words</h2>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>The Cosmic Ledger</dt><dd>The Framework's name for the running total of residue left by every collapse in the history of the universe. Readable only as a balance.</dd>
      <dt>Residue polarisation</dt><dd>The directional trace a collapse is held to leave behind when one outcome is kept and the rest are not.</dd>
      <dt>Phased integration</dt><dd>The teaching that matter and energy stand at levels of integration, and that moving between them is what a phase change is.</dd>
      <dt>Scale factor</dt><dd>The single number <em>a</em> describing how much space has stretched. Densities fall as powers of it, which is why the mixture changes.</dd>
      <dt>&#937; (omega)</dt><dd>A component's density as a fraction of the critical density. The three fractions on this page are omegas.</dd>
      <dt>Coincidence problem</dt><dd>The unresolved question of why we happen to live in the narrow window when matter and dark energy are comparable.</dd>
      <dt>Running coupling</dt><dd>The measured fact that interaction strengths depend on the energy at which they are probed.</dd>
      <dt>No-cloning</dt><dd>The theorem that an unknown quantum state cannot be copied. One of the real limits the Ledger leans on.</dd>
      <dt>The Two Infinities Framework</dt><dd>James Alexander Matthew Rankin's independent research project: the Moebius Seam, the Cosmic Ledger and the Rankin Skeletal Splice as one account, written out in full as the Unified Edition. Where this site and that account differ, that account is correct.</dd>
      <dt>Rankin Skeletal Splice</dt><dd>The arithmetic limb of the Framework: the fork taken at every density threshold, the halves sent back counted as R<sub>n</sub> = F<sub>n+2</sub> &minus; 1, and the deposit per density that converges on &phi;&sup2;/&radic;5 = 1.170820393&hellip;</dd>
      <dt>Quantum of deposit</dt><dd>&phi;&sup2;/&radic;5, the amount of accumulated polarisation each density adds in the limit. It makes progress linear in n, which makes the tick 1/n, which makes the ascent unfinishable.</dd>
      <dt>&chi;-field</dt><dd>The Framework's bookkeeping of how far a region has travelled along &alpha; &rarr; &pi; &rarr; &pi;/2 &rarr; i. &chi; &asymp; 0 is dark energy, &chi; &asymp; &frac12; is dark matter, &chi; &asymp; 1 is ordinary matter.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

